---
// src/pages/legal/terms-of-use.astro
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that govern use of the Ember Ridge website, a ministry of Firebrand Revivalists."
  updated="[DATE TO BE SET AT LAUNCH]"
  intro="Plain terms for the use of this website. They are not a substitute for the agreements that govern guest stays, gifts, or professional services."
>
  <h2>Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    By using this website you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not
    use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>About the content on this site</h2>
  <p>
    This website describes a ministry in formation. Descriptions of property, buildings,
    renovations, budgets, timelines, programs, and staffing are plans and intentions
    based on current information. They are not offers, guarantees, or commitments, and
    they may change as due diligence, professional review, funding, and the leading of
    God direct.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site is an offer to sell or a solicitation to buy any security or
    interest in property.
  </p>

  <h2>No professional relationship</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this site is offered for information and spiritual encouragement. It is
    not legal, financial, tax, medical, psychological, or other professional advice, and
    using this site or contacting us does not create an attorney-client, counseling,
    pastoral care, or other professional relationship. See our
    <a href="/legal/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your use of the site</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the site unlawfully or to harm others</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the site or its systems</li>
    <li>Interfere with the operation or security of the site</li>
    <li>Submit false, abusive, threatening, or intentionally misleading information</li>
    <li>Scrape, harvest, or reuse content or contact information for commercial purposes</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Submissions</h2>
  <p>
    When you send us a message, prayer request, referral, or other material, you confirm
    that you have the right to share it. You grant us permission to read, retain, and act
    on it for ministry purposes as described in our
    <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>. If your message concerns another
    person, please share only what is necessary and appropriate.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The Ember Ridge and Firebrand Revivalists names, logos, marks, written content,
    photographs, and design of this site are owned by the ministry or used with
    permission. You may share links and quote short excerpts with attribution. Please ask
    before reproducing substantial content, and do not use our names or logos in a way
    that suggests endorsement or affiliation.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>[Needs legal review:</strong> confirm trademark status of the Ember Ridge and
    Firebrand Revivalists marks, and confirm licenses and photo credits for all imagery
    used on this site.<strong>]</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    We may link to other websites. We do not control them and are not responsible for
    their content or practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We provide this site “as is.” We do not promise uninterrupted availability or that
    the site will be free of errors, and we may change or remove content at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>[Needs legal review:</strong> insert a limitation of liability and indemnity
    clause appropriate to North Carolina law and the ministry’s insurance coverage. Do
    not publish this page without counsel completing this section.<strong>]</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of North Carolina, without regard
    to conflict-of-law principles. <strong>[Needs legal review:</strong> confirm venue
    and dispute-resolution preference.<strong>]</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. Continued use of the site after an update means you accept
    the revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
